IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g6-nouns`
IMPORT `g6-notice-and-hearing`
IMPORT `g6-appeal-and-publication`

-- ind-c-tests-appeal.l4: independent tests (ind-c) of ss.55-57 (gazette pp. 196-197).
-- Scenario ids are those of work/ind-c/expectations.md.

§ `ind-c: ss 55 to 57`

§§ `Fixtures`

`no rest days` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS EMPTY

GIVEN days IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A `Calendar of rest days`
`rest on` days MEANS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS days

`ind-c individual` MEANS Person WITH `reference for the person` IS "ind-1", `kind of person` IS `an individual`

GIVEN what IS A `Listed violation`
      act IS A STRING
GIVETH A Violation
`ind-c violation of` what `by the act` act MEANS
    Violation WITH `the violator` IS `ind-c individual`
                 , `the listed violation` IS what
                 , `reference for the act` IS act
                 , `date of the act` IS YMD 2027 3 10

GIVEN statesIntention IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Notice of intention`
`ind-c a notice announcing the name:` statesIntention MEANS
    `Notice of intention` WITH
        `delivered on` IS YMD 2027 3 1
        `in writing` IS TRUE
        `states the act or omission that is the breach and the date of the breach` IS TRUE
        `states the amount of the sanction` IS TRUE
        `the period for payment the notice states, in days` IS JUST 30
        `states the violator's right to make representations under section 43` IS TRUE
        `states that the notice will be treated as a payment demand if the right is not used` IS TRUE
        `states the power to add for a continuing or repeat violation and the rate of the addition` IS TRUE
        `states the intention to publish the violator's name` IS statesIntention

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      isPublished IS A BOOLEAN
      barredA IS A BOOLEAN
      omittedB IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Item of a publication under section 57(a)`
`ind-c item` n `published` isPublished `barred by 9(a)` barredA `omitted under 9(b)` omittedB MEANS
    `Item of a publication under section 57(a)` WITH
        `the item number` IS n
        `published` IS isPublished
        `barred from disclosure by section 9(a) of the Freedom of Information Law` IS barredA
        `omitted because section 9(b) of the Freedom of Information Law does not oblige disclosure` IS omittedB

§§ `E1-E2: s 55, one sanction for one act`

-- E1: one act ("act-A") that constitutes two listed violations; a sanction was imposed for one of them: no second.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 55 — a financial sanction may still be imposed for` (`ind-c violation of` `engaging a person who had no licence at all` `by the act` "act-A") `given` (LIST (`ind-c violation of` `work with no licence at all` `by the act` "act-A")) `and` FALSE)
-- A different act: no bar.
#ASSERT `s 55 — a financial sanction may still be imposed for` (`ind-c violation of` `engaging a person who had no licence at all` `by the act` "act-B") `given` (LIST (`ind-c violation of` `work with no licence at all` `by the act` "act-A")) `and` FALSE
-- E2: the act was already sanctioned under another law: none under this Law.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 55 — a financial sanction may still be imposed for` (`ind-c violation of` `engaging a person who had no licence at all` `by the act` "act-B") `given` EMPTY `and` TRUE)
-- The invariant: two sanctions for act-A break it.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 55 — no act has more than one financial sanction among` (LIST (`ind-c violation of` `work with no licence at all` `by the act` "act-A"), (`ind-c violation of` `engaging a person who had no licence at all` `by the act` "act-A")))
#ASSERT `s 55 — no act has more than one financial sanction among` (LIST (`ind-c violation of` `work with no licence at all` `by the act` "act-A"), (`ind-c violation of` `engaging a person who had no licence at all` `by the act` "act-B"))

§§ `D27-D31: s 56, the appeal`

-- D27: notice of the decision delivered Tuesday 2027-06-01: 45 days, last day Friday 2027-07-16; 2027-07-17 is late.
#ASSERT `s 56(a) — the last day of the 45 days from` (YMD 2027 6 1) `with` `no rest days` EQUALS YMD 2027 7 16
#ASSERT `s 56(a) — the day` (YMD 2027 7 16) `is within the period to appeal that runs from` (YMD 2027 6 1) `with` `no rest days`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 56(a) — the day` (YMD 2027 7 17) `is within the period to appeal that runs from` (YMD 2027 6 1) `with` `no rest days`)
-- D28: Friday 2027-07-16 and Saturday 2027-07-17 both rest days: Sunday 2027-07-18 (the module's reading A).
#ASSERT `s 56(a) — the last day of the 45 days from` (YMD 2027 6 1) `with` (`rest on` (LIST (YMD 2027 7 16), (YMD 2027 7 17))) EQUALS YMD 2027 7 18
-- D29: delivered 2027-06-02: nominal last day Saturday 2027-07-17, a rest day: 2027-07-18.
#ASSERT `s 56(a) — the last day of the 45 days from` (YMD 2027 6 2) `with` (`rest on` (LIST (YMD 2027 7 17))) EQUALS YMD 2027 7 18
#ASSERT `s 56(a) — without s 10(c), the last day of the 45 days from` (YMD 2027 6 2) EQUALS YMD 2027 7 17
-- D30: filing does not stay the decision unless the Commissioner agreed or the court ordered.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 56(b) — the filing of the appeal stays the execution of the decision, given` FALSE `and` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 56(b) — the filing of the appeal stays the execution of the decision, given` TRUE `and` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 56(b) — the filing of the appeal stays the execution of the decision, given` FALSE `and` TRUE
-- D31: paid 20,000, the court reduced the sanction to 15,000: 5,000 is returned, with shekel interest (an input).
#ASSERT `s 56(c) — the amount to be returned of` 20000 `when the court reduced the sanction to` (JUST 15000) EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `s 56(c) — the amount to be returned of` 20000 `when the court reduced the sanction to` NOTHING EQUALS 20000
#ASSERT `s 56(c) — the amount returned with shekel interest` 5000 `and` (JUST 120) EQUALS 5120

§§ `F1-F6: s 57, publication`

-- F1/F2: the items required: (1), (2), (3), (5) always; (4) after a reduction; (6), the name, for a corporation only.
#ASSERT `s 57(a) — the numbers of the items the Law requires where` FALSE `and the violator is` `an individual` EQUALS LIST 1, 2, 3, 5
#ASSERT `s 57(a) — the numbers of the items the Law requires where` FALSE `and the violator is` `a corporation` EQUALS LIST 1, 2, 3, 5, 6
#ASSERT `s 57(a) — the numbers of the items the Law requires where` TRUE `and the violator is` `a corporation` EQUALS LIST 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6
-- F3: an individual's name: only if necessary to warn the public AND after an opportunity to argue; the s.43
-- hearing counts only if the notice of intention announced the intention to publish the name.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 57(c) — the Commissioner may publish the name of the violator` `an individual` `who was given a separate opportunity:` FALSE `by the notice of intention` (`ind-c a notice announcing the name:` FALSE) `the Commissioner thinking publication necessary to warn the public:` TRUE `and the name being barred by section 9(a):` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 57(c) — the Commissioner may publish the name of the violator` `an individual` `who was given a separate opportunity:` FALSE `by the notice of intention` (`ind-c a notice announcing the name:` TRUE) `the Commissioner thinking publication necessary to warn the public:` TRUE `and the name being barred by section 9(a):` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 57(c) — the Commissioner may publish the name of the violator` `an individual` `who was given a separate opportunity:` TRUE `by the notice of intention` (`ind-c a notice announcing the name:` FALSE) `the Commissioner thinking publication necessary to warn the public:` TRUE `and the name being barred by section 9(a):` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 57(c) — the Commissioner may publish the name of the violator` `an individual` `who was given a separate opportunity:` TRUE `by the notice of intention` (`ind-c a notice announcing the name:` TRUE) `the Commissioner thinking publication necessary to warn the public:` FALSE `and the name being barred by section 9(a):` FALSE)
-- F4: an item s.9(a) bars must not be published; an item s.9(b) covers may be left out.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 57(a), (d) — the item is dealt with as the Law requires` (`ind-c item` 5 `published` TRUE `barred by 9(a)` TRUE `omitted under 9(b)` FALSE) `where it is required:` TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 57(a), (d) — the item is dealt with as the Law requires` (`ind-c item` 5 `published` FALSE `barred by 9(a)` TRUE `omitted under 9(b)` FALSE) `where it is required:` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 57(a), (d) — the item is dealt with as the Law requires` (`ind-c item` 2 `published` FALSE `barred by 9(a)` FALSE `omitted under 9(b)` TRUE) `where it is required:` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 57(a), (d) — the item is dealt with as the Law requires` (`ind-c item` 3 `published` FALSE `barred by 9(a)` FALSE `omitted under 9(b)` FALSE) `where it is required:` TRUE)
-- F6: published 2027-05-10: an individual's through 2029-05-10, a corporation's through 2031-05-10 (a Saturday; kind
-- V, no s.10(c)).  On 2029-05-11 the individual's period is over.
#ASSERT `s 57(e) — the last day of the publication period that began on` (YMD 2027 5 10) `for` `an individual` EQUALS YMD 2029 5 10
#ASSERT `s 57(e) — the last day of the publication period that began on` (YMD 2027 5 10) `for` `a corporation` EQUALS YMD 2031 5 10
#ASSERT `s 57(e) — the day` (YMD 2029 5 10) `is within the publication period that began on` (YMD 2027 5 10) `for` `an individual`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 57(e) — the day` (YMD 2029 5 11) `is within the publication period that began on` (YMD 2027 5 10) `for` `an individual`)
#ASSERT `s 57(e) — the day` (YMD 2029 5 11) `is within the publication period that began on` (YMD 2027 5 10) `for` `a corporation`
